%% Sequence: user sends a message, failure paths. Normal path: send-message.mmd.
%% Rules and timers: docs/SEND_MESSAGE.md.
sequenceDiagram
  actor U as User
  participant B as Browser (SPA)
  participant A as API (FastAPI, Fargate)
  participant DB as Postgres (Neon)
  participant R as AgentCore runtime

  alt Access token expired
    B->>A: POST /sessions/{id}/messages (expired token)
    A-->>B: 401 token_expired
    B->>A: POST /auth/refresh (cookie)
    alt refresh token valid
      A->>DB: rotate refresh token
      A-->>B: 200 new access token
      B->>A: resend with the same clientMessageId (no duplicate message)
    else refresh token expired, revoked or reused
      A->>DB: reuse detected → revoke the whole token family
      A-->>B: 401 session_expired
      B->>U: "Auth expired" screen, draft kept in the browser
      U->>B: Continue with Google → sign-in, then resend
    end

  else Agent marked offline
    B->>A: POST /sessions/{id}/messages
    A->>DB: agent status offline
    A-->>B: 503 agent_unavailable (JSON, no stream) · nothing saved
    B->>U: composer disabled, draft kept, past sessions readable

  else A reply is already running in this session
    B->>A: POST /sessions/{id}/messages
    A-->>B: 409 run_in_progress · nothing saved

  else Agent unreachable when called
    A->>R: InvokeAgentRuntime
    R-->>A: error (not found, throttled, 5xx, timeout)
    A->>DB: assistant message status failed, error code
    A-->>B: event run.failed {code, retryable} · stream closes
    B->>U: "Reply failed" + Retry (reruns the same user message)

  else Agent error mid-stream
    R-->>A: error event, or the stream breaks
    A->>DB: keep partial blocks, status failed
    A-->>B: event run.failed · stream closes
    B->>U: partial reply + "Reply failed" + Retry

  else User presses Stop
    U->>B: Stop button or Esc
    B->>A: POST /sessions/{id}/runs/{runId}/stop
    A->>R: cancel (close the AgentCore stream)
    A->>DB: keep partial blocks, status stopped
    A-->>B: event run.stopped · stream closes
    A-->>B: 200 (stop request)
    B->>U: partial reply marked "Stopped"

  else Browser disconnects (network drop, tab closed, laptop sleeps)
    B--xA: connection lost
    Note over B: Client also treats 45 s with no bytes<br/>(3 missed pings) as a lost connection
    A->>A: stop writing SSE · the agent task keeps running (D11)
    loop until the agent finishes or the 15-min cap
      R-->>A: chunk
      A->>DB: checkpoint
    end
    A->>DB: status complete (interrupted if the cap was hit)
    B->>U: banner "Connection lost. The agent is still working"
    B->>A: on reconnect or reload: GET /sessions/{id}/messages
    loop every 2 s while status is streaming
      B->>A: GET /sessions/{id}/messages/{messageId}
    end
    B->>U: full reply (or "Interrupted" + Retry)

  else API task stops mid-reply (deploy, crash)
    Note over A: SIGTERM: refuse new streams, let open ones finish (up to 120 s, P2)
    A--xB: task killed before the reply finished
    Note over A,DB: On next start, rows still "streaming" become "interrupted" (P1)
    B->>A: lost connection → poll GET /sessions/{id}/messages/{messageId}
    B->>U: partial reply + "Interrupted" + Retry
  end
